# Frontend conventions
- Use `docs/core-scope/04_flows-to-screens.md` for screen responsibilities. Use `docs/design/01_design-concept.md` for visual styling. The current palette is Light Mint & Indigo.
- Keep presentation separate from API calls: shared API client plus feature-specific services.
- Put colours in one shared token set (CSS variables). Components use token names, not hard-coded hex, so the palette can change without restyling each screen. The MVP ships that one palette; it does not include a theme picker.
- Use a simple, responsive layout with header navigation. Do not inherit CareerContext styling.
- Reuse a straightforward Markdown editor/preview pattern where relevant; sanitise/render user content safely.
- Handle loading, empty, validation, and AI-failure states explicitly.
- Keep question keys, rubrics, and grading data out of the active quiz player until submission.
- Build accessible forms and keyboard-friendly quiz inputs; avoid premature UI frameworks/abstractions.
